The preferred solution is indeed wtgms.f2[!is.na(wtgms.f2)], as I
posted.  Your solution works by coercing wtgms.f2 to character, and
than checking if the coerced value is "NA".  This is inefficient, and
does not work correctly with NaNs: (S-PLUS 6.0)

> x <- c(1, NA, 0/0)
> x
[1]  1 NA NA
> is.na(x)
[1] F T T
> x != "NA"
[1] T F T

