Answer: win.test[,3] is a single column and is automatically converted to a
vector.A vector has no "dim" attrribute and hence no "dimnames" attribute so
the name is lost.The same would happen if you specified a single column to
bind with logicals. Hence to be safe, you may have to assign the dimnames
(or names , if its a dataframe) attribute explicitly.

win.new<-cbind(win.add[,good],win.test[,2:3]) WOULD, however, keep the
correct names (mod possible duplication of names, of course) for the same
reasons.

