> > os> win.new
> > one two a b e X3

Bert is absolutely correct: win.test[,3] is a vector, and so the column name
is lost.  But on the other hand, win.test[,3,drop=F] is a data frame with a
single column named "three", so

win.new <- cbind(win.test[,1:2], win.add[,good], win.test[,3,drop=F])

would also produce the desired result with the correct names.

The drop=F trick is also handy for extracting a 1-row or 1-column matrix
from a larger matrix, preserving the dimnames.

