From hatfield at solander.bc.ca  Thu Dec  7 15:06:40 2000
From: hatfield at solander.bc.ca (Todd Hatfield)
Date: Thu, 07 Dec 2000 07:06:40 -0800
Subject: Thanks for the slope comparison
Message-ID: <5.0.2.1.0.20001207064742.02cc4080@solander.bc.ca>

Many thanks to Jason Connor, Eric Zivot, Matthew Zack, Joseph Bevene, Paul 
Lin, Rolf Turner and Ed Jones for patiently demonstrating how to run a 
t-test on regression coefficients.  The answer is:

(coeff - 0) / s.e.(coeff) ~ t(df)

This tests how different the coefficient is from 0. To test against other 
slopes, you simply need to replace the "0" with the other

number.

Thank you all very much!

Cheers, Todd Hatfield

